WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:01.935
Tonight, Taraji

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:03.837
P Henson's brutally honest

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.538
and emotional explanation

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.239
of Hollywood's

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:08.174
pay disparity is going viral.

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:10.243
CNN host Gayle King interviewed Henson

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.312
and the cast of The Color Purple.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:14.381
It's a film from CNN's parent company,

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:15.715
Warner Brothers Discovery.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.317
Now, King asked Henson

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.619
if she was thinking about quitting acting

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:25.992
I'm just tired

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.761
of working

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.898
so hard

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:34.534
being gracious at what I do.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.603
Getting paid a fraction of the cost.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.372
You get tired I hear people call.

00:00:39.372 --> 00:00:40.440
You work a lot.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:42.809
You have to the mayor.

00:00:42.809 --> 00:00:44.411
Thank my friend.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:46.613
Here to discuss this

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:46.946
with me

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:49.382
now is actress Yvette Nicole Brown.

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:50.583
Yvette,

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:53.053
that has really touched a nerve

00:00:53.353 --> 00:00:54.788
in Hollywood.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.122
She's been

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.892
Taraji has been nominated for an Oscar.

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:01.661
She's had multiple Emmys, Screen Actors

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.329
Guild Awards.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.198
She's a household name.

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:06.099
It's surprising

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.033
to a lot of people

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.502
to see those tears and to hear her say

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:11.805
she's not being paid fairly.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:14.374
Yeah, I

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:16.576
mean, the truth is, none of us are.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.977
You know, the pay disparity

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.412
for black women,

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.680
period, is horrible

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.816
and it extends to Hollywood as well.

00:01:22.816 --> 00:01:23.316
What broke

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.851
my heart about seeing it is

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.886
that Taraji is one of our treasures.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:27.353
You know what I mean?

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.154
She's one of the ones

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:28.721
that has been

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.557
in the trenches for forever.

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.659
She should be paid what she's worth.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:33.960
And the tears as she cried

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.462
they weren't just for her.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:36.296
Because each of us

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:37.897
that are further along in our careers,

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:38.832
we're trying to leave the door

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:40.533
open for every black actresses

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:41.534
coming up behind us.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.303
And the fear that she had

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:45.071
and the despair that she had was that

00:01:45.071 --> 00:01:46.806
she is not making enough to be able

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:47.340
to tell them

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.842
what they should be asking for.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:50.643
And she knows that if it's hard for her,

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.145
even harder for them.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:53.713
So it just it broke my heart

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:54.280
and I think that's

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:54.914
why everybody's

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.649
been responding and chiming in

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:57.383
and making sure

00:01:57.383 --> 00:01:58.384
she knows that we love her

00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:59.419
and we support her

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:00.487
and that we're walking the same

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:01.955
path with her. Yeah.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.223
I want to play a little bit

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:04.791
to what you were talking about here,

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:05.325
about what she

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.493
said in a separate interview.

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:09.963
Where's my race?

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:10.663
I am I

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.565
haven't seen a raise in my income,

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:15.802
says Proud Mary.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.305
And almost had to walk away from Color

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.841
Purple. Because, you know what?

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.977
If I don't take a stand,

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.146
how am I making it easy for Fantasia?

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:29.582
And Danielle, Haley and Phylicia?

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.285
So why am I doing this

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:33.353
if it's all just for me?

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:36.422
What the why are you here?

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:39.292
Pay in any industry

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.060
in some ways is very subjective.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.762
I can only imagine in Hollywood

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.864
it's even more so.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:48.067
What do you think is the reason that,

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.270
you know, Hollywood

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:52.338
executives get away with paying

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.040
someone like Taraji less

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.341
and not giving her a raise movie

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:57.911
to movie role to roll?

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:58.912
Well, you know, systemic

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.046
racism is a part of

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:01.814
everything that happens in this nation.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:02.916
But beyond that,

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.117
I think that there's this thing

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.585
where they pick people against each other

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.020
where the idea is, well,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:07.220
you know,

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:07.921
if you don't want to do it,

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.622
we'll get somebody else to do it

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:11.524
and somebody won't maybe do.

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.593
And so they may take the lesser amount.

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:16.563
And we are we are lesser as a as a

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:17.931
as an industry,

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:18.665
because we don't get

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:19.332
to have the brilliance

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:20.333
of someone as Taraji

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:21.467
because they don't want to pay them

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.302
what they're worth.

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:23.236
And it's a fight that,

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:23.603
you know,

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:25.071
white actors don't have and white

00:03:25.071 --> 00:03:26.706
female actors don't have.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:27.407
And what she said

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.408
that really resonated with me,

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:29.742
Abby, was when she said

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:30.743
even if she fights

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:31.911
and gets what she needs

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.546
for this particular film,

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.881
she has to start all over again.

00:03:34.881 --> 00:03:36.549
The next time she gets a film

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.917
because you don't get to walk in.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.586
Well, I negotiated this, this and this.

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:40.653
And I am Taraji

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.155
P Henson, and I have this Oscar

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.289
nomination, whatever.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.657
Now it's like you starting over

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.092
and you just walked in and, well,

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:46.793
you know, we're going to give you

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.628
this $5 in a volunteer.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:50.430
It's the same for all of us.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.932
And it's infuriating and exhausting.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:55.301
One of the factors here,

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:55.902
the Color Purple,

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.103
she just said in that clip,

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.705
she almost walked away from that film.

00:03:58.705 --> 00:03:59.205
That's a film

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:00.173
that is near

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:00.473
and dear

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.341
to the heart of Oprah

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:04.277
Winfrey is a part of that process.

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:07.647
Does it surprise you to hear that

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:09.782
even on a film like that,

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.050
where there is a prominent

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.086
black woman as a part of the process

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:14.020
of making it,

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:14.988
that she could still feel

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:15.822
that she was underpaid?

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.323
Taraji, we're showing here,

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:19.726
posted a photo of Oprah thanking her

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:22.362
for supporting her throughout her career.

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:24.530
But what do you make of that event?

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.198
Well well,

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:25.932
we don't know

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:27.333
if if Oprah had anything

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:29.002
to do with the pay situation.

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:29.736
So we can't say

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.137
that she was warring against

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:32.605
anything that Oprah did in particular.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.440
So I want to make sure I say that

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.441
I think a lot of times

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:37.510
it comes from business affairs.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.045
You talk to your friends,

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:39.946
we're going to do this movie

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:41.281
or this TV show together.

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:42.081
And then by the time

00:04:42.081 --> 00:04:42.949
it gets to the lawyers

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:44.584
negotiating everything

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:46.152
that you and your friend decided

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:47.053
or you discussed

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:49.756
gets torn down by the legal process.

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.724
So sometimes it's it's

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:52.825
the people in the legal department.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.694
Like we're not giving it to a trailer.

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:55.495
Wait a minute. You know?

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:56.095
And so

00:04:56.095 --> 00:04:57.897
we never know where the breakdown is,

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:59.165
but we know that the breakdown

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:00.566
happens every time.

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:02.468
This is not an isolated incident.

00:05:02.468 --> 00:05:04.437
Her tears are not just her tears.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:05.571
We all have cried then.

00:05:05.571 --> 00:05:07.540
We all are fighting to make it better.

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:07.840
And again,

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:08.474
it's not even just

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:09.375
entertainment industry.

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:10.443
You can talk to any system

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.045
that's working in any industry.

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:14.347
And we have to always fight harder.

00:05:14.347 --> 00:05:15.548
It's just the way it is.

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:16.883
And we're tired of it

00:05:16.883 --> 00:05:18.718
being that's just the way it is.

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:22.055
You know, even someone who it seems

00:05:22.055 --> 00:05:24.357
almost everybody knows who she is

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.758
still fighting these battles.

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:26.626
Yvette, Nicole Brown,

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:28.628
thank you so much for joining us on this.

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:30.563
Thank you for having me.

